Vitamin D helps the body absorb calcium and phosphorus and supports bone health by aiding calcium retention in the kidneys (NHS: https://www.nhs.uk/medicines/colecalciferol/about-colecalciferol). It is found in oily fish such as salmon, mackerel, trout, sardines, pilchards and herring, as well as in egg yolks, meat, milk, and added to margarine and some breakfast cereals (NHS: https://cios.icb.nhs.uk/health/nutrition/vitamin-d). The recommended daily amount for adults in the UK during autumn and winter is 10 micrograms (NHS: https://cios.icb.nhs.uk/health/nutrition/vitamin-d).

